{
 "manufacturer": "Yaskawa",
 "manufacturer_slug": "yaskawa",
 "model": "E7 HVAC drive (CIMR-E7U) - Modbus RTU",
 "model_slug": "e7",
 "short_model": "E7",
 "aliases": [
  "CIMR-E7U",
  "E7U",
  "E7 Drive"
 ],
 "equipment_type": "Variable frequency drive (HVAC)",
 "applies_to": "Yaskawa E7 (CIMR-E7U) HVAC fan and pump drives using the built-in RS-422/485 terminals with H5-08 = 0 (Memobus/Modbus), per Parameter Access Technical Manual TM.E7.11 (rev 3016).",
 "summary": "The E7 is Yaskawa's legacy HVAC fan/pump drive with a built-in RS-422/485 port that speaks Memobus/Modbus RTU (or Metasys N2 / APOGEE FLN). All registers are hex: commands at 0001h-000Fh, detailed fault and alarm words from 0010h, status from 0020h, U1/U2/U3 monitors from 0040h, and every parameter at its own address. This map covers the command block, all status/fault words, the main monitors with their published units, and the b1/H5 communication parameters.",
 "transport": [
  "RTU"
 ],
 "defaults": {
  "unit_id": 31,
  "baud": 9600,
  "parity": "None",
  "data_bits": 8,
  "stop_bits": 1,
  "tcp_port": null
 },
 "addressing": {
  "convention": "hex 0-based",
  "note": "All addresses are hex and go into the request unchanged: the manual's read example sets starting register 00h 20h to read 0020h-0023h. Parameters use the hex address in the parameter table (b1-01 = 0180h, H5-01 = 0425h). ENTER/ACCEPT are printed as 900/910, i.e. 0900h/0910h."
 },
 "default_word_order": null,
 "firmware": "Manual revision 3016",
 "source": {
  "title": "E7 Drive Parameter Access Technical Manual",
  "doc_number": "TM.E7.11",
  "revision_date": "2004-05-31",
  "url": "https://www.yaskawa.com/delegate/getAttachment?documentId=TM.E7.11&cmd=documents&documentName=TM.E7.11.pdf",
  "pages": "Ch. 1 pp. 1-8 to 1-10 (comm parameters), Ch. 2 p. 2-4 (03h example), Ch. 4 pp. 4-3 to 4-10 (command, broadcast, monitor registers), pp. 4-12 and 4-17 (b1, H5 parameters), p. 4-21 (ENTER/ACCEPT)"
 },
 "notes": [
  "0040h/0041h frequency monitors are printed as 'Units 0.01Hz' in TM.E7.11, but the E7 user manual (TM.E7.01) says frequency monitor units change with o1-03; they are left unscaled here. 0002h frequency reference likewise depends on the display-unit setting.",
  "Left out because the sign is not stated: 0028h/0032h torque, 0047h/0033h output power, 0063h-0065h PID input/output/setpoint, 0068h heatsink temperature, 0051h Iq, and 0038h-003Ah PID levels (no units printed in TM.E7.11).",
  "0011h operator status and 0012h OPE bits and 0013h product code are not included.",
  "Fault code numbers for U2-01/U3-01 are not tabulated in TM.E7.11, so no value list is given.",
  "Broadcast (slave 0): 0001h bit 0 run, bit 1 reverse, bits 5/6 multi-function inputs S3/S4, bits C-E S5-S7 (enabled by 000Fh bits C-E); 0002h frequency reference fixed at 30000 = 100 % of maximum frequency.",
  "The register map comes from TM.E7.11; the E7 user manual TM.E7.01 Appendix D gives the same data-table layout.",
  "From the free E7 user manual TM.E7.01 (Appendix D, https://www.yaskawa.com/delegate/getAttachment?documentId=TM.E7.01&cmd=documents&documentName=TM.E7.01.pdf): 8 data bits and 1 stop bit, up to 31 slaves, ENTER/RAM-only registers 0900H/0910H, and no fault trace for CPF00, CPF01, CPF03, UV1 and UV2."
 ],
